    "preamble": "N. Anusha vs The State Of Telangana on 13 June, 2025",
    "facts": "3. The case of the petitioner is that she was appointed as a Food Safety Officer in 2020 and has been discharging her duties without any complaints. On 07.01.2025, respondent No.4 issued a memo based on a news telecast dated 19.12.2024, alleging that the petitioner collected money from traders in Rajanna Sircilla District, and sought an explanation. The petitioner submitted a detailed reply on 09.01.2025, denying all allegations and clarifying that one Sanjeev, a retired employee, had collected the amount. On the same day, respondent No.2 also issued a provisional seniority list for the post of Gazetted Food Inspector (Multizone-I), wherein the petitioner was placed at Serial No.3. However, she was not considered for promotion, while one T. Sunitha, placed at Serial No.4, was promoted vide Procdgs.Rc.No.5596/E1/IPM/Estt/2025, dated 02.05.2025. As such, the petitioner submitted a representation dated 08.05.2025, but no action was taken. Aggrieved by the same, the petitioner filed the present Writ Petition.",
